WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.767
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:04.868
You're here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:07.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
"Tonight Show."

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:09.534
Well, guys, big news
around the building today.

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:11.767
The new Rockefeller Center
Christmas tree

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:13.501
has been selected.

00:00:13.501 --> 00:00:16.667
And, yeah, it's an
80-foot-tall Norway spruce

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:18.968
from Upstate New York.
Yeah.

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:20.734
And the tree is 80 feet tall

00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:23.100
or 81 feet
in Ron DeSantis's heels.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.701
[ Laughter ]
And --

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:27.667
It's exciting.
Let's get to some news here.

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:30.601
Today, following
Donald Trump Jr.'s testimony,

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:33.501
Eric Trump took the witness
stand in the civil fraud trial

00:00:33.501 --> 00:00:36.033
against his dad.
Oh, it was really cute.

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:37.834
Eric still had a little green
makeup on his face

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:40.133
from his Hulk costume.
Yeah, it was cute.

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:42.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:44.100
It's actually convenient
that all the Trumps

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.667
have testified now,
because they're going to use

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:47.734
the courtroom sketches
for their holiday card,

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:49.801
and I think that's smart.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:52.701
I think it's touching.
Yeah.

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:54.901
Hey, I want to say congrats
to the Texas Rangers,

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:59.334
who just won their first
ever World Series.

00:00:59.334 --> 00:01:03.167
Congratulations.
[ Applause ]

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:05.133
It's very exciting.
And after the game,

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:08.334
MLB commissioner Rob Manfred
went down to the field

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.534
to congratulate them.
Let's see how that went.

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:13.901
-[ Voice cracking ] 63 years
is a long time to wait,

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:18.200
but the Texas Rangers
are World Series champions.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:22.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.601 --> 00:01:24.467
-It was a busy time
for the commissioner.

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:26.367
In one night, he celebrated
the World Series

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:28.400
and, apparently,
his 13th birthday.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.334
And I think that's very...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.334 --> 00:01:32.033
[ Laughs ]

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:34.067
[ Voice cracking ]
"They played great."

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:37.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:39.467
"I'm McLovin, and..."

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:41.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.300
[ Normal voice] Well, guys,
it's been a week

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.033
since Congress elected
a new speaker of the House,

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:47.033
and he's not the most
famous guy in Washington,

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:48.767
but we've all had a week
to get to know him,

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:50.434
which means it's time
to play that classic game

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:52.367
"What's the Speaker's Name?"

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:55.534
-"What's the Speaker's Name?"!

00:01:55.534 --> 00:01:57.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:57.868 --> 00:02:01.234
-All right. The game is simple.

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:03.601
I'm going to ask you, "What is
the House speaker's name?",

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:06.501
and to help you out,
here is a photo.

00:02:06.501 --> 00:02:09.200
All right.
There he is.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.901
Okay, Tariq, you're up first.
What is the speaker's name?

00:02:12.901 --> 00:02:15.100
-Uh, I want to say Greg Smith.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.200
[ Buzzer ]

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.167
-Ah, not quite.
Quest, you're up.

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:19.501
Tell us, what is
the speaker's name?

00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:22.267
-Damn.
I was gonna say Greg Smith.

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:23.567
Roger Stevens?

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:25.601
[ Buzzer ]
-Oh, I'm afraid not.

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:27.534
Mark, your turn.
What is the speaker's name?

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:29.534
-I think I've got it.
Is it Mark Kelly?

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:31.100
[ Buzzer ]
-Ooh, that's --

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:33.567
That's your name, Mark.
-I knew it sounded familiar.

00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:34.801
[ Laughter ]
-All right.

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:36.300
Let's try this again.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.734
He's the third most powerful
person in the United States.

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.634
What is his name, Tariq?

00:02:40.634 --> 00:02:41.701
-Nancy Pelosi.

00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:43.767
[ Buzzer ]
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:45.767
-George Santos.
[ Buzzer ]

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:47.501
-Tim Speaker.
[ Buzzer ]

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:49.968
-You think the House speaker's
last name is "Speaker"?

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:51.067
-I do, yes.

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:52.534
[ Thunder crashes ]

00:02:52.534 --> 00:02:53.634
-Ooh, guys, you know
what that means.

00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:55.534
It's time
for the lightning round.

00:02:55.534 --> 00:02:57.701
And I'll even accept
his first name only.

00:02:57.701 --> 00:02:59.033
Ready, go!

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:00.734
-Carl!
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:00.734 --> 00:03:01.767
-Uh, Tom!
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:01.767 --> 00:03:03.434
-Tim.
-No! Keep trying.

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:05.033
-Kevin.
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:06.167
-Nick.
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:07.400
-Brian!
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.734
-A.J.
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:09.767
-Howie!
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:09.767 --> 00:03:11.033
-No, those are
the Backstreet Boys.

00:03:11.033 --> 00:03:12.667
-Chase!
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:14.267
-Marshall!
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:15.434
-Rocky.
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:15.434 --> 00:03:16.434
-Skye!
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:17.901
-No, those
are "Paw Patrol" dogs.

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:21.601
[ Sad tuba plays ]
Oh, that sound...

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:25.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:25.968 --> 00:03:29.968
That sound means
that we're out of time.

00:03:29.968 --> 00:03:32.868
I'm afraid none of you
could guess the speaker's name.

00:03:32.868 --> 00:03:34.634
-Jimmy! Jimmy!
Can I guess?

00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:37.634
-Uh, yeah, sure.
You in the audience, go for it.

00:03:37.634 --> 00:03:40.067
-Is it Greg Smith?

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:41.300
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.567
-They already guessed that.

00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:44.868
I'm so sorry.
What is your name, sir?

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:47.801
-Me?
I'm Mike Johnson.

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:49.334
-That's it!
That's the speaker's name --

00:03:49.334 --> 00:03:52.067
Mike Johnson!
Catch me!

00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:53.634
-Oh! Whoa!

00:03:53.634 --> 00:03:56.434
Stop tickling me!
Oh! Oh!

00:03:56.434 --> 00:04:00.501
Oh! Oh!
Crowd surf! Crowd surf!

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:02.267
Let's go!

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:20.868
♪♪

00:04:20.868 --> 00:04:23.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:29.667
-[ Breathing heavily ]

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:31.601
Anyway, in other news, um...

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:33.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:36.167
You guys hear about this?
Today, The Beatles

00:04:36.167 --> 00:04:38.200
released a new song
called "Now and Then,"

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:41.200
features all four members
of the band.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.901
Yeah, for younger viewers
who don't know

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:44.200
how huge the Beatles were,

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.601
just imagine four Taylor Swifts
in matching suits.

00:04:46.601 --> 00:04:49.434
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:04:49.434 --> 00:04:52.067
That's who they are.

00:04:52.067 --> 00:04:53.868
Well, the the fifth
and final season

00:04:53.868 --> 00:04:56.033
of "Stranger Things"
is still in the works,

00:04:56.033 --> 00:04:58.868
and the producer says
that they will not use A.I.

00:04:58.868 --> 00:05:02.100
to de-age the actors
and make them look younger.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:05.067
He thinks that they can
still pass off as kids.

00:05:05.067 --> 00:05:07.767
I don't know.
Take a look at the trailer.

00:05:11.501 --> 00:05:14.133
-School's out, and it's time
for one last adventure

00:05:14.133 --> 00:05:15.467
with the whole gang.

00:05:20.767 --> 00:05:22.934
And of course, Eleven.

00:05:27.601 --> 00:05:30.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
I don't know.

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:36.601
Some more TV news.

00:05:36.601 --> 00:05:39.467
Paramount just announced
two new "Yellowstone" spinoff

00:05:39.467 --> 00:05:44.033
series, called
"1944" and "2024."

00:05:44.033 --> 00:05:45.567
Basically, at every
Paramount pitch meeting,

00:05:45.567 --> 00:05:47.501
someone tosses out a year, and
the boss is like, "Let's do it."

00:05:47.501 --> 00:05:50.067
[ Laughter ]
"Sounds good."

00:05:50.067 --> 00:05:52.367
I saw that, this week,
both Starbucks and Dunkin'

00:05:52.367 --> 00:05:54.300
debut their holiday menus.
-Oh.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:55.734
And it's --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:55.734 --> 00:05:59.400
Yeah, but it's very interesting
to compare the two chains.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:00.934
I mean, take a look
at the Starbucks

00:06:00.934 --> 00:06:02.601
holiday menu announcement here.

00:06:02.601 --> 00:06:04.634
-'Tis the season at Starbucks.

00:06:04.634 --> 00:06:08.334
Stop in today for a peppermint
mocha or caramel brulée latte

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:10.133
and taste the holiday spirit.

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:13.934
-Yeah. That's nice.
Now let's see Dunkin's.

00:06:13.934 --> 00:06:16.434
-Christmas is almost here,
bitch.

00:06:16.434 --> 00:06:19.334
Get your ass over here
and suck down a frappa mocha.

00:06:19.334 --> 00:06:20.667
Who gives a [bleep]

00:06:20.667 --> 00:06:22.868
And we'll throw in
a free pack of Marlboros.

00:06:23.834 --> 00:06:27.200
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:29.601
I just...

00:06:29.601 --> 00:06:31.868
I just find that interesting.

00:06:31.868 --> 00:06:33.801
Hang on. There's
another Starbucks video.

00:06:33.801 --> 00:06:34.834
Let's check this out.

00:06:34.834 --> 00:06:36.767
-Did someone say eggnog?

00:06:36.767 --> 00:06:40.000
You will "nog" be able
to resist our egg-nog latte.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.100
[ Giggles ]

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:44.000
Try one today at Starbucks.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.701
-I love that, you know?
Let's see.

00:06:45.701 --> 00:06:47.334
Can we see Dunkin's now?

00:06:47.334 --> 00:06:48.701
-Did someone say egg nog?

00:06:48.701 --> 00:06:50.634
Well, they should shut
their frickin' mouth.

00:06:50.634 --> 00:06:51.934
It's still November.

00:06:51.934 --> 00:06:54.267
We got watery coffee
and some old spider doughnuts

00:06:54.267 --> 00:06:55.467
we got to get rid of.

00:06:56.267 --> 00:06:58.968
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:06:58.968 --> 00:07:00.601
-We're getting word.
There's another one.

00:07:00.601 --> 00:07:01.934
-Really?
-Here's another one --

00:07:01.934 --> 00:07:03.467
another one from Starbucks.

00:07:03.467 --> 00:07:06.100
-There's no need to attack
our menu offerings.

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:10.300
We are just trying to spread
holiday cheer at Starbucks.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:12.934
-Oh, spare me that
holier-than-thou crap, Donna.

00:07:12.934 --> 00:07:14.767
You're just bitter
'cause I never called you back

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:16.434
after we hooked up.
Dunkin'.

00:07:16.434 --> 00:07:18.634
-[ Chuckles ]
He's lying.

00:07:18.634 --> 00:07:20.934
I would never.
Starbucks.

00:07:20.934 --> 00:07:23.167
-Oh, come on, Donna,
don't gaslight me. Dunkin'.

00:07:23.167 --> 00:07:24.634
-Oh, shut up, Ronnie.
It meant nothing,

00:07:24.634 --> 00:07:26.701
and you friggin' know it.
Starbucks.

00:07:26.701 --> 00:07:28.634
-Donna, oh, my God!
Don't you dare

00:07:28.634 --> 00:07:31.400
tear my heart out like this!
Donn-a-a-a-a!

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:33.334
-Happy holidays
from Tim Hortons. Sorry.

00:07:33.334 --> 00:07:37.234
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]
-Now -- okay.

00:07:37.234 --> 00:07:39.234
I -- Now I know what it is.
I get it.

00:07:39.234 --> 00:07:41.400
[ Applause ]

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:43.701
Hey, listen to this.
Today, the FDA proposed

00:07:43.701 --> 00:07:47.501
banning a harmful chemical
that is added to many sodas.

00:07:47.501 --> 00:07:49.801
Yeah, and one guy chugging
Mountain Dew Code Red was like,

00:07:49.801 --> 00:07:51.334
"Wait. This isn't
organic Code Red?"

00:07:51.334 --> 00:07:52.901
[ Laughter ]

00:07:52.901 --> 00:07:54.634
"I'm used to
farm-to-table Mountain Dew."

00:07:54.634 --> 00:07:56.300
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:57.701
Guys, well, get this.
A 13-year-old

00:07:57.701 --> 00:08:00.834
just broke a world record
by popping 20 balloons

00:08:00.834 --> 00:08:03.834
suspended from a rotating pole
in under a minute,

00:08:03.834 --> 00:08:07.167
while doing backwards
somersaults on a trampoline.

00:08:07.167 --> 00:08:09.300
[ Laughter ]

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.934
Wait a minute.
Is -- Is that true?

00:08:11.934 --> 00:08:15.400
-Wait.
What's wrong, Jimmy?

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:17.300
I knew this day was gonna come.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:18.300
Sad piano.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:19.868
[ Sad piano music plays ]

00:08:19.868 --> 00:08:21.033
[ Laughter ]

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:23.834
-What's --
What's going on with you?

00:08:23.834 --> 00:08:25.400
-Dramatic spotlight.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:26.901
[ Laughter ]

00:08:26.901 --> 00:08:28.167
-Wait, wait.

00:08:28.167 --> 00:08:30.434
Is this about the kid
breaking the world record?

00:08:30.434 --> 00:08:34.100
-Yeah. I just -- I thought
it wouldn't happen so soon.

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:35.901
I thought I'd have more time
to savor the view

00:08:35.901 --> 00:08:37.501
from the mountaintop, you know?

00:08:37.501 --> 00:08:38.734
-Well, yeah, sure,
if you're the one

00:08:38.734 --> 00:08:40.334
who held the previous re--

00:08:40.334 --> 00:08:44.734
Wait a minute.
Did that kid break your record?

00:08:44.734 --> 00:08:46.868
-Yeah, he did.

00:08:46.868 --> 00:08:49.667
Once it was I who was
the toast of the town,

00:08:49.667 --> 00:08:51.367
the guy on the trampoline

00:08:51.367 --> 00:08:53.400
who popped balloons
with an ease and grace

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:55.000
that few could
even dream of doing.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.567
And then along comes a kid
who stole it all from me,

00:08:57.567 --> 00:08:59.100
just like that.
[ Snaps fingers ]

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.200
Took me decades
to master that trick.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.501
Years of my life,
skipping dental appointments,

00:09:03.501 --> 00:09:07.133
birthdays, holidays,
more dental appointments,

00:09:07.133 --> 00:09:10.234
colonoscopies,
more dental appointments.

00:09:10.234 --> 00:09:11.434
I put my life on the line

00:09:11.434 --> 00:09:13.300
in a never-ending quest
to be the king,

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:16.133
and now I have to decide
if I want to stay down

00:09:16.133 --> 00:09:18.667
like a boxer who's been punched
too many times in the face,

00:09:18.667 --> 00:09:20.734
or do I want to pick myself
up off the mat

00:09:20.734 --> 00:09:22.300
and go another round?

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:25.267
Do I even have the fire in me
for another fight?

00:09:25.267 --> 00:09:28.767
Is the lion inside me too tired
to protect his throne?

00:09:28.767 --> 00:09:31.934
-Well, what are you gonna do?

00:09:31.934 --> 00:09:34.901
-[ Breathes deeply ]

00:09:37.834 --> 00:09:39.834
I'm gonna take back
what's mine.

00:09:39.834 --> 00:09:41.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:43.467
-Yes!

00:09:43.467 --> 00:09:45.100
-Mark my words.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:46.868
I'm coming for you, kid!

00:09:46.868 --> 00:09:49.367
Because I'm about
to pop 21 balloons

00:09:49.367 --> 00:09:52.133
while suspended from a rotating
pole in under a minute

00:09:52.133 --> 00:09:55.634
while doing backwards
somersaults on a trampoline!

00:09:55.634 --> 00:09:59.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:59.868 --> 00:10:02.133
Moving on.

00:10:02.133 --> 00:10:03.567
And finally,
a new study found

00:10:03.567 --> 00:10:07.534
that cats have 276 different
facial expressions.

00:10:07.534 --> 00:10:09.167
Yep, 276 expressions,

00:10:09.167 --> 00:10:10.667
and they're all
subtle variations

00:10:10.667 --> 00:10:12.868
of "Get away from me."
We have a great show.

00:10:12.868 --> 00:10:15.968
Give it up for The Roots,
everybody!

